# Cloudflare Pages header rules
# https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Deliberately NOT here: X-Frame-Options. Umami heatmaps work by loading the
# live page in an iframe from stats.jeffyclassify.com, so a blanket DENY would
# break them. frame-ancestors below allows exactly that one origin and nothing
# else, which is the same protection without the collateral damage.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self' https://stats.jeffyclassify.com
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# No long cache TTLs anywhere. We deploy often and have no purge-on-deploy
# hook, so a long TTL just serves stale content to most visitors. Cloudflare's
# default (max-age=0, must-revalidate) already revalidates on every request and
# still saves the bytes via 304, which is the behaviour we want. If we ever add
# a cache purge to the deploy step, revisit.

# Importable n8n workflows: fetched cross-origin from n8n, so allow that.
/blog/n8n-jeffy/*.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
